ly  other option is for him to track down  the newly reincarnated version of  treadway  and find out where he put it the film is  really a two-hour long easter egg hunt  the problem is the man who has been  imbued or reincarnated with treadway's  soul doesn't know he has it  at a young age his visions were  misdiagnosed as schizophrenia and he was  put on medication he even tried  committing suicide via car crash which  resulted in him getting a steel plate  inserted into his head  a plot point which becomes pivotal later  on in the film to pay for his medication  evan played here by mark wahlberg who  has the soul of treadway in him  makes samurai swords for local drug  dealers you know normal things  he doesn't quite know how he has this  ability he just knows how to do it  because he was once a japanese  blacksmith in a previous life  he even retains all his knowledge from  those past lives making him a walking  wikipedia  homeboy knows anything you freak but  when the drug deal goes wrong and evan  finds himself running from the cops he's  brought into police custody where  bathurst and the nihilists have tracked  him down  apparently both the nihilists and  believers have an entire network that's  been searching for him and when a  samurai sword forged in a style  unseen since edo japan popped up on  their radars they knew they had a  potential match  the only problem is evan has no idea  about his past even when a gun is pulled  on him notice treadway's ring here which  is the same ring his past-life self wore  in the 1985 intro segment it's only when  evan touches a slingshot from one of his  past lives that he gets a quick  flashback of him as a mayan or aztec  warrior the interrogation is cut short  when nora brightman one of the leaders  of the believers  crashes the party quite literally and  escapes with evan he decides to join her  thinking that this whole event is one  psychotic episode none of this is real  it's a psychotic break is that easier to  believe in the idea that maybe destiny  has something more in store for you  fun easter egg here are the license  plates this one here says reincarnate  and the one from 1985 says infinite  unsuccessful in his attempt at acquiring  the egg we see bathurst being  waterboarded  this has never explained why someone  would want to do this on purpose but the  fact he says  god show me your face leads me to  believe he wants to bring himself closer  to death  in order to get closer to god near the  end of the film when he finally does  acquire the egg he wonders out loud if  god will stop him after all he's about  to destroy the entire planet unlike the  other infinite who develop their  memories of their previous lives as they  grow  older and over time bathurst gets them  all at once as soon as he's developing  in the womb he says the flood of these  memories at once eat away at him and  it's unbearable no wonder he wants to  stop it evan is taken to the hub the  main base of the believers where they  attempt to bring his memories back  now you may think there would be tons of  these infinites around but there aren't  treadway has created a gun-like device  called the dethroner which stores the  soul of its victims restricting them  from entering a new host  essentially he's created a gun that can  lock an infinite in a pseudo-cyber  prison over 200 believers are locked  away in there this is the same gun we  see him use in the intro against a man  named abel nora's partner for hundreds  of years  she tells him to meet her in the  beginning which is their code word for  anchor watt but with abel's soul  imprisoned nora is left to live out the  rest of eternity without her  partner the meeting at the hub also sets  up two important threads  one that treadway had abnormal powers  that no one could understand  he can manipulate the energy of the  world around him this is what evan will  later use to stand upright on the plane  in the final act but other than this  there's no explanation as to why  treadway has this power or where it came  from  second the believers keep the bodies of  their previous hosts and will soon find  out what the real reason for this is  hint it's not to keep as souvenirs the  believers are unable to unlock evan's  memories and must venture to london to  meet a man known as the artisan who  might be able to help  but in order to get them unlocked evan's  brain will need to be jump-started which  can only be done via drowning and  bringing him back to life  it's only when his life literally  flashes before his eyes that he realizes  treadway buried the egg inside his own  body  and conveniently that body is still  stored at the hub  but bathurst says it already sees  control and taken the body with the egg  in it to scotland now it's never  explained why he just doesn't start the  device right here and now probably  because if he did there wouldn't be a  third act so evan and nora go after  bathurst with evan making an  insane motorcycle leaf off a cliff onto  the plane whereby the motorcycle falls  into the engine really just screwing up  bathurst's plans and as evan is about to  destroy the egg which has been put in  this creepy box thing for some reason  he's shot with the dethroner by bathurst  but remember how evan had that steel  plate in his head  the bullet hits and doesn't work which  results in this insane samurai skydiving  battle where  evan stops the bomb and successfully  imprisons bathurst using his own  gun meanwhile the artisan and nora blow  up the imprisoned souls along with a  gravely wounded nora  she fought one of the bathurst minions  and was injured this explosion will  allow those souls to be  released the last we see of evan is him  falling into the ocean from the plane we  aren't sure what happens to him  until the final scene we're in jakarta  indonesia roughly 15 years later  the artisan has tracked down a young boy  with an amazing proficiency for sword  fighting he believes him to be the  reincarnation of treadway which would  mean  evan died and this is confirmed when the  boy says what took you so long  see you soon treadwell but the more  heartwarming ending is nora finally  reuniting with her love with both her  soul  and her partners released by the  explosion in scotland we see  two young people holding hands at angkor  wat or what abel and nora called the  beginning ironic since this is the end  of the movie  now if you want my personal opinion of  the movie it was a total 5 out of 10  action flick that brought nothing new to  the genre it felt like a hodgepodge of  other movies pasted together with no  real intriguing character to root for  so unless you have a paramount plus  account i'd say this movie is a pass  thanks for watching everyone be sure to  like subscribe and comment every little  bit helps the channel out  for more bad takes you can follow me on  twitter and instagram thinkstoryyt  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much  you
 

